LC 11 — Container With Most Water
attern

Two PointersLogic
Start at both ends.
Area = width × smaller height
Move the pointer with the smaller height.

Algorithm:
Calculate area.
Update maximum area.
Move the shorter pointer.
Return maximum area.

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    int maxArea(vector<int>& h) {
        int l = 0, r = h.size()-1, ans = 0;
        while (l < r) {
            ans = max(ans, min(h[l], h[r]) * (r-l));
            if (h[l] < h[r]) l++;
            else r--;
        }
        return ans;
    }
};

EX:
height = [1,8,6,2,5,4,8,3,7]

l=0, r=8 → area = 8×1 = 8
Move l

l=1, r=8 → area = 7×7 = 49 ✅
Move r

Maximum area = 49
